text:
zoe: linkbot flagged a handful of function-calling examples that still show the old invoke signature. I'll open a PR to modernize them.

ravi: thanks — I can update snippets to `redwood.calls.invoke({ tool, input })` and add a one-line shim for backward compatibility.

ken: please also fix the JSON envelope sample so it includes an explicit "tool" field and mark "results" as nullable. our parser tests blew up on the current sample.

ravi: noted. quick snippet I'll swap in the PR:
```js
// new pattern used in docs
const out = await redwood.calls.invoke({
  tool: 'search',
  input: { q: 'cats' }
})
// optional legacy shim
function invokeTool(name, input) {
  return redwood.calls.invoke({ tool: name, input })
}
```

zoe: also run the link-checker after you push, linkbot found a couple redirects to `/docs/legacy-toolcalls`.

linkbot: Scan summary: scanned 4 pages under /docs/function-calling + /docs/structured-output — found 2 broken links: /docs/legacy-toolcalls (404) and /images/schema-old.png (410). Recommend updating inline links and adding redirects.

ken: add a tiny defensive parsing example too, e.g. `const items = resp.results ?? []` and tolerate `metadata` being null. customers appreciate one-liners.

ravi: will include. PR branch `docs/fncall-refresh` in ~25m. ping here when it's up and I'll run CI checks.

zoe: perfect, tag me on the PR and I'll add a short release-note mention.
